<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Technihire yr share up 20 pct, div rises.</title>
<headline>Technihire yr share up 20 pct, div rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, pre-excepts (cts) 13.58     vs   11.30</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		   5.0	vs    4.0</p>
<p>    Retained income	   1.09     vs    0.93</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		     2.86     vs    2.24</p>
<p>    Tax			   1.13     vs    0.81</p>
<p>    Interest received	 0.17     vs    0.07</p>
<p>    Turnover		   11.81     vs   13.09</p>
<p>Div payable: July 11</p>
<p>On register: June 20</p>
<p>Full name: Technihire Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the outlook for the coming year and growth in earnings was expected to continue. A new financial services division was being introduced which should be of benefit to both clients and contractors, it said.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
